<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pau Claris</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1586–<a href="/years/1641">1641</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pau Claris was a Catalan cleric, canon of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-seu-durgell">La Seu d'Urgell</a>, who was president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/generalitat-de-catalunya">Generalitat of Catalonia</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reapers-war">Reapers' War</a>. As a royal army advanced on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a>, he proclaimed a Catalan Republic under French protection in January 1641, and days later placed Catalonia under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiii-of-france">Louis XIII of France</a>. He died suddenly in February 1641.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pau-claris.jpg" alt="Pau Claris" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antoni Castelucho Vendrell · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pau_Claris_-_La_Ilustraci%C3%B3_Catalana_-_1880.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
